## COMPARISON: PARALLEL vs SEQUENTIAL

### Parallel Processing (Port 8098)
- Purpose: Speed optimization
- Method: Simultaneous entity extraction + vector embedding
- Use Case: Fast document processing
- Average Time: 25.3 seconds per document

### Sequential Processing (Port 8099)
- Purpose: Knowledge graph construction
- Method: Step-by-step entity → embedding → relationship pipeline
- Use Case: Structured knowledge extraction
- Average Time: 2.06 seconds per document

## DATABASE SCHEMA

### Tables Created
```sql
-- Parallel processing results
legal_documents_extracted (entities, embedding, processing_time_ms)

-- Sequential knowledge graphs
knowledge_graphs (entities, embeddings, relationships, graph_stats)
```

### Indexes
- GIN indexes on JSONB fields for fast queries
- Document ID indexes for retrieval
- Vector indexes for similarity search

